          "id": "f3845bd54eb2b3d47cbe7066f0367903333827ec",
          "message": "tests: Automatically shut down the one-shot server after some time (#10714)\n\nThe one-shot server automatically terminates after serving one single\r\nHTTP request, which is useful for tests. Unfortunately, if no such\r\nrequest happens, e.g. due to something else in a test failing so the\r\nrequest never happens the tests currently leave a one-shot werserver\r\ninstance running indefinitely.\r\n\r\nIt is hard to know whether a test is still going to happen or not but\r\nthis PR adds a timeout for the server that if nobody connects for a set\r\namount of time the server will terminate on its own.\r\n\r\nThis limits the left-behind servers which will automatically terminate\r\non their own after a while when nobody connects.\r\n\r\nSigned-off-by: Marek Kubica <marek@tarides.com>",
